Now EnrollmentService — the core. Design:

```java
@Service
public class EnrollmentService {
    private final EnrollmentRepository repo;
    private final RandomNumberAllocator allocator;
    private final AuditRepository audit;
    private final TransactionTemplate txTemplate;
    private final Clock clock;
    private final SecureRandom random = new SecureRandom();

    public EnrollmentResponse enroll(String trialCode, EnrollmentRequest req) {
        try {
            return txTemplate.execute(status -> doEnroll(trialCode, req));
        } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
            return resolveAfterDuplicate(trialCode, req);
        }
    }
    ...
}
```

doEnroll:
- trial = repo.findTrialByCode → 404 TRIAL_NOT_FOUND
- center = repo.findCenterByCode → 404 CENTER_NOT_FOUND
- fingerprint = sha256(requestId|screeningNo|centerCode|consentSignedAt.toString())
- existing = findByRequestId → if fingerprint equal → replay response; else throw conflict REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT
- byScreening → conflict SUBJECT_ALREADY_ENROLLED
- randomNo = allocator.allocate(...)
- repo.lockCounter(...)
- arm = blockArm(...)
- insert enrollment
- audit ENROLLED (actor null, detail "randomNo=...")
- return response(replayed=false)

resolveAfterDuplicate (runs outside tx, read-only):
- trial lookup again
- existing = findByRequestId: if found: fingerprint equal → replay; else conflict REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT
- else if findByScreening != null → conflict SUBJECT_ALREADY_ENROLLED
- else rethrow generic conflict

blockArm(trial, center, randomNo):
- blockNo = (randomNo-1)/4, pos = (randomNo-1)%4
- arm = findBlockArm; if null → generateBlock → re-read
- return char

generateBlock(trialId, centerId, blockNo):
- prev = blockNo > 0 ? blockArms(blockNo-1) : empty
- arms = ['T','T','C','C'] shuffled
- if prev.size()==4 && prev[2]==prev[3] && arms[0]==arms[1]==prev[2] → fix: find index i in 2..3 with arms[i] != prev-last, swap arms[0] and arms[i]... wait need arms[0..1] not both equal to prevLast. If arms[0]==arms[1]==prevLast, then arms[2..3] are both the other arm. Swap arms[1] with arms[2] → first two become [prevLast, other]. Good deterministic fix.
- try insertBlock catch DuplicateKeyException → ignore (concurrent generated; re-read)

Note: catching DuplicateKeyException from insertBlock inside the transaction — H2 allows continuing the tx after constraint violation. OK.

